From f9c51fad76e201e4f2a1e3bf7e27cb2c065dd3c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:27:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Add image OCR for image-only Telegram posts, and
 date/timestamp on headlines

- image_ocr.py (new): local OCR via pytesseract (eng+hin) for Telegram posts
  that are a photo/screenshot with little or no caption text. These were
  previously dropped silently because the extraction pipeline only ever read
  post text. OCR output is fed into the same post["text"] field so it flows
  through the existing extraction/dedup/merge pipeline unchanged.
- pipeline.py: parse_telegram_html now detects a post's photo (Telegram
  renders it as a CSS background-image, not <img src>) and keeps image-only
  posts instead of dropping them; collect() runs OCR on them before the
  length/age filter. Never breaks the run if tesseract isn't installed.
- .github/workflows/pipeline.yml: install tesseract-ocr + tesseract-ocr-hin
  on the runner.
- requirements.txt, sources.yml, .env.example: new pytesseract/Pillow deps
  and ocr_enabled/ocr_languages/ocr_min_chars/ocr_max_per_run settings.
- app.js, index.html: show a date/timestamp against every headline in the
  main feed, Saved tab, and the country story viewer.
